-- title:
--   Globalising a level-N structure to an Eichler order
-- statement:
--   Let $r,\bar r$ be primes with $\bar r \neq r$ and let $N \geq 1$ be a squarefree natural number divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$. Let $a_1,b_1 \in \mathbb{Q}$ be such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a₁ b₁ rbar`, i.e. $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$, and for every height one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completion $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_w$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $\bar r \in w$. Let $v$ be a height one prime containing $r$, let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ which is an order (contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, $\mathbb{Q}$-spans the algebra, and is finitely generated), and let $\Lambda_1$ be a maximal order (an order not properly contained in any order). Assume that for each $w \neq v$ there is a unit $u$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ with $\mathrm{localBox}(R,w) = u\,\mathrm{localBox}(\Lambda_1,w)\,u^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{localBox}(\Lambda,w)$ denotes the additive subgroup of the completion generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_w$. Assume further given a $\mathbb{Z}$-linear map $\varphi : R \to M_2(\mathbb{Z}/N)$ which sends $1$ to $1$, is multiplicative, is surjective, and satisfies $\varphi(x)=0$ if and only if $x \in N\cdot R$; and let $R_0 \leq R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule such that an element $x$ of $R$ lies in $R_0$ exactly when the $(1,0)$ entry of $\varphi(x)$ vanishes. Then there exist $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules $\Lambda'$ and $R'$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ such that $\Lambda'$ is a maximal order, $R'$ is an Eichler order of level $N$ in the sense that $R' = \Lambda'_1 \cap \Lambda'_2$ for two maximal orders with the relative index of the additive group of $R'$ in that of $\Lambda'_1$ equal to $N$, $R' \leq \Lambda'$, and for every $w \neq v$ one has $\mathrm{localBox}(R',w) = \mathrm{localBox}(R_0,w)$ and $\mathrm{localBox}(\Lambda',w) = \mathrm{localBox}(R,w)$.
--
--   This is the local-to-global step that converts an order which is locally conjugate to a maximal order away from the place $v$, together with a surjection onto $M_2(\mathbb{Z}/N)$ playing the role of a level-$N$ structure, into an honest Eichler order of level $N$ inside a maximal order with prescribed completions away from $v$. It feeds the construction of the fake elliptic curve moduli data in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the argument.
-- source:
